// title: TTP Detection Rule: NetSupport running from unexpected directory (FIN7) · Defender XDR
// date: 2026-10-21
// product: Defender for Endpoint
// tables: DeviceProcessEvents
// purpose: Detection opportunity: NetSupport running from unexpected directory In the instances where the adversary delivered NetSupport Manager RAT as a follow-on payload, our existing detection coverage for malicious NetSupport installation served us well. Under normal circumstances, you should expect NetSup
// source: https://github.com/Bert-JanP/Hunting-Queries-Detection-Rules/blob/65d11700e1cb878403d87312acdd6b9a8dd622c1/Defender%20For%20Endpoint/ttp_t1219_netsupportrat_fin7.md
// kind: repo
// author: Bert-Jan Pals
// license: BSD-3-Clause (as stated by the repository)
// archived by tools/kql_archive.py (CLAUDE.md 5l, 5eu)
// Detection opportunity 2: NetSupport running from unexpected directory
DeviceProcessEvents
| where ( ProcessVersionInfoCompanyName contains "netsupport" or ProcessVersionInfoProductName contains "netsupport" ProcessVersionInfoCompanyName contains "Crosstec" or ProcessVersionInfoProductName contains "Crosstec") and not ( FolderPath has_any ("Program Files (x86)\\","Program Files\\"))
